# The wire-contract fixture is byte-significant: `tests/plugin_wire_contract.rs`
# compares the core's serialized output against these exact bytes. Git must not
# rewrite its line endings on checkout, or the test fails on any platform with
# `core.autocrlf` enabled.
tests/fixtures/plugin_wire_contract/changelog_request.json -text

# The request goldens in `tests/fixtures/plugin_requests/` are byte-significant for
# the same reason, and more strictly: `tests/plugin_request_goldens.rs` compares them
# to the bytes the host writes to a plugin's stdin, including the absence of a
# trailing newline. A checkout that appends CRLF fails the test on the developer's
# git configuration instead of on the contract.
tests/fixtures/plugin_requests/*.json -text
